WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.960
(lively music)

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.310
- Los Angeles.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:06.060
Good views. Here we are, Beverly Hills.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.079
Bad traffic,

00:00:07.079 --> 00:00:07.912
(horns beeping)

00:00:07.912 --> 00:00:10.230
so many electric vehicle chargers.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.570
Charger number one, two, three.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.900
From the streets of downtown
to the beach in Santa Monica,

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.900
11, 19 23, we visited 30
DC fast charging locations,

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.650
none of them run by Tesla.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.770
28, 29, 30.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:29.007
That meant more than 100
different charging stalls.

00:00:29.007 --> 00:00:30.240
(chargers clicking)

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.910
There was just one little problem.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.200
Yeah, this one's broken.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.630
Broken and also broken.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.730
Okay, many problems.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.550
Come on, you can do it.
Connect to the ve...

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:42.840
Error detected.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.280
There's nothing on the screen.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.160
I've tried putting my
credit card in every way.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.740
At just over 40% of
the charging locations,

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.780
I encountered problems.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.520
Yeah, not good.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.920
As the US moves to an
electric vehicle future,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.390
LA is ahead of it all, but oh
boy, are things a mess here.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:04.350
What can we learn from it
all and can it be fixed?

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.383
All right, let's go test
a whole bunch of chargers.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:10.459
Here's how we set up this test.

00:01:10.459 --> 00:01:11.970
(upbeat music)
(electricity buzzing)

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.730
Los Angeles County has
more DC fast chargers

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.920
than any other place in the country.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.470
So over two days, I tried to go to as many

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.500
as I could in a Rivian R1T.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.760
Why the Rivian?

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.320
Well, it's awesome

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:28.290
unless you're trying to
enter a parking garage.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:29.763
Okay, duck down.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.700
I'm totally aware that
ducking does nothing.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.250
Plus, like the majority of non-Tesla Evs,

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.560
it has a CCS charging port.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.870
When you've got that port
and you need to charge,

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.760
a DC fast charging station,

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.170
typically an EVgo

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:46.230
or Electrify America is your best bet,

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:49.110
except those stations,
according to my testing,

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:51.930
have three main problems.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:53.434
Number one, out of order.

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:55.080
(playful music)

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:59.040
I inspected 126 charging stalls in total.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.940
27% of those stalls were
just flat out of order.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.230
That is they had a sign

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:07.680
or an error that said charger
unavailable, out of service.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.270
So it works.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.070
EVgo, Electrify America

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.590
and EVCS all told me that they quickly try

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:17.760
to fix these issues by deploying
technicians to the sites.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.890
But honestly, I preferred this issue

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:21.360
because it saved me from the hassle

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.300
of trying the charger and then failing.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.975
Which brings me to number two, payment.

00:02:27.975 --> 00:02:29.310
(electricity buzzing)

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:33.210
Nearly 10% of the stalls
visited had payment issues.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:37.680
It says cash only. Where would I put cash?

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:41.070
Yes, there were specifically
repeated credit card problems.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:42.870
Why are you beeping at me?

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.570
Present card again.
(machine beeping)

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.970
Okay, nope. Let's see if this will work.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:52.170
Now it's telling me to swipe
the card. Present card again.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:56.850
Swiping card, present card
again. Try another card.

00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:01.410
Wiping my other card. Nope, nothing.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.480
EVCS said these issues can arise

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.130
because the payment hardware is made

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:07.350
by a different company than the charger.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:10.890
EVgo said paying by app is
a more seamless experience,

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:14.520
and I found that app paying was
better for all the chargers.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.140
Some EVs and charging companies

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.090
even support plug and charge.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.950
So it just starts charging your account

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:21.930
when you plug into your car.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.360
But you still have to set those apps up.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.850
Why don't you take Apple Pay?

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.670
Number three, connection issues.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:32.010
Even if the payment works,

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.200
it is connecting now to my vehicle.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.553
Can you two connect?

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:41.070
Charger meet Rivian. Rivian meet charger.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.590
Connect. Error detected.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:46.080
This may be the most
frustrating one of all,

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:49.380
when the car and the charger
don't connect to each other,

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.810
what many call the handshake issue.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.300
Basically, when you plug
the charger into the car,

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.860
the two have to talk to each other

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.720
and send information about voltage

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.000
and energy levels back and forth.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.210
And a lot can go wrong in this process.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:04.890
I'll get to more of that soon.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.750
Sometimes the charger will prompt you

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.550
with ways to troubleshoot.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:09.870
Please unplug the connector.

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:13.200
Wait 10 seconds, plug in
the connector and try again.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:16.530
I will try to unplug and
replug like a router,

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:18.540
but it doesn't always work.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.520
And to be fair, this handshake issue

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.170
isn't just a Rivian thing.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:26.095
I've experienced this problem
on many different EVs.

00:04:26.095 --> 00:04:27.690
(lively music)

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:30.150
To find out why this is
all such a broken mess,

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.520
I met up with ChargerHelp,
an LA-based company

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.860
that attempts to clean up the mess.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:37.320
So you fix chargers.
- Yes.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.024
- There are a lot of broken chargers.

00:04:39.024 --> 00:04:41.100
- Yeah, no, we fix a
lot of chargers in LA,

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:43.680
especially with our LA
technicians that we have here.

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:45.930
- Sergio, one of the
ChargerHelp technicians,

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.360
walked me through fixing one stall.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:50.040
- It shows that it has a fault here.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.930
So a power cycle of the unit,

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:55.510
we can go ahead and hit
the breaker to shut it off.

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:56.343
(lever clicking)

00:04:56.343 --> 00:04:58.170
- [Joanna] Yep, as
simple as turning it off

00:04:58.170 --> 00:04:59.473
and turning it on again.

00:04:59.473 --> 00:05:01.290
(charger clicking)

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:03.570
- So we're getting the
green prompt lights,

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:06.960
which means the charging
station is back online.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:09.330
- [Joanna] But most
repairs are not that simple

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.920
because again, the car

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:13.050
and the charger are computers that have

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:15.000
to communicate with each other.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.920
- [Sergio] This is the
whole motherboard here,

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:20.370
which sometimes goes bad
and we have to replace.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:21.810
- [Joanna] Sergio explained that this set

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.840
of cables connect from the
motherboard to the charger

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.550
to communicate with the car.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.710
It's that handshake I mentioned before.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:32.070
The charger tells the car
how much voltage it can send

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:35.400
and the car says, "Hey,
here's how much I can accept."

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.560
But that's where things can break down.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.910
- Sometimes the network where you're at,

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:41.220
whichever area you're in, it's poor.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:42.840
So you have to try it multiple times.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.010
So it actually ends up working,

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.960
if you notice, when you try like the third

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:48.090
or fourth time, it ends
up actually working.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:51.360
- [Joanna] And remember, the
DC fast chargers I tested

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.400
have to communicate with
lots of different types

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.860
of electric vehicles,
which is why things can get

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.890
so much more complicated
than on Tesla's network.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.810
- So it's one station trying to figure out

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:01.650
how to communicate

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:03.810
with multiple different types of firmware.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.340
Whereas if you have a Tesla system,

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.800
it's a vertically integrated
where they have a car,

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.902
a station, and a payment
system that's all together.

00:06:10.902 --> 00:06:11.910
(lively music)

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.239
- So what's the future of EV charging?

00:06:14.239 --> 00:06:15.300
(electricity buzzing)

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.990
Starting in 2024, Tesla's
opening up its charging network,

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:21.240
allowing cars from Rivian, Ford, and GM,

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:24.090
and others to charge at Tesla stations.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:26.460
Doesn't fit, at least not yet.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:27.660
Eventually, those car companies

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:30.750
will also adopt Tesla's
NACS charging port.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:34.740
Will it be total hassle-free
charging? I'm not so sure.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:38.160
Tesla is only used to
charging their own cars

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.460
and those other DC fast
charging stations from EVgo,

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:44.820
Electrify America and more
should get better too.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:46.800
At an EVgo station in Santa Monica,

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.290
I got to try out some
newer charging stalls.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:53.130
It says checking cable
safety, matching voltage.

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:55.560
This tells you what it's doing.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.063
These new machines are great.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.190
Representatives from each

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:00.990
of the charger companies told me many

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:04.350
of the issues I encountered
were because of legacy hardware

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:06.330
and that they are constantly upgrading,

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:09.479
which we actually saw at
this Electrify America.

00:07:09.479 --> 00:07:10.620
(Joanna knocking)

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.350
Knock knock. Is there a charger in there?

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:14.670
Plus, in September,

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:17.490
the Biden administration
opened up $100 million

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:19.920
in federal funding to repair and replace

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:23.160
existing electric vehicle
charging infrastructure.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:25.920
That's in addition to
the $5 billion program

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:29.250
to help states build out
more EV charging sites,

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:31.440
which should help with the lines.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:35.640
Excuse me, are you guys
almost done charging?

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:38.910
So what did I learn here
over the last few days?

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:41.220
Well, if you can, charge at home

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:44.640
or your hotel, yet I met many travelers

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:47.730
and apartment renters who
don't have that option.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:50.190
Really? What I learned is patience.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:53.010
Have a lot of it when pulling
into one of these stations

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:54.780
and understand that this isn't as simple

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:57.690
as plugging your phone into the wall.

00:07:57.690 --> 00:08:00.450
Oh, and avoid credit
cards whenever possible.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:03.390
Just use that charger's mobile app.

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:07.290
But if LA is any sign,
this EV revolution is going

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:11.010
to feel more like a slow, messy evolution.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.083
Charging. Woo-hoo.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:15.790
At least that's what it says.

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:23.373
20, we hit 20. You like this
dance? It's really cool.

